 # Trigger synthetic receive turn with a direct batch message
 
-When tattler_receive has requested delivery and pending inbox is non-empty, defer until the session is idle, drain pending messages with the shared batch helper, and trigger the receive turn with the canonical batch custom message itself. Avoid sending a fake user prompt solely to reach before_agent_start, because sendCustomMessage(triggerTurn=true) bypasses that hook. Guard against reentrancy from inside awaited agent_end listeners.
+After tattler_receive terminates and agent_end fires, defer until idle (zero-timeout/idle polling) before draining the pending inbox with the shared helper and calling pi.sendMessage(batchCustomMessage, { triggerTurn: true }). Do not use sendUserMessage because it renders as the human user. Avoid reentrancy during agent_end handler dispatch and avoid Operation Aborted semantics.
 
